Feature: Recovery of orders in Created state
  As a system administrator
  I want orders in Created state to be properly recovered
  So that the system can maintain consistent state after restart

  Background:
    Given the system is in recovery mode
    And the transaction logs are available

  Scenario: Order in Created state is rebuilt
    Given an order with ID "ORD-123" exists in transaction logs
    And the order has state "Created" in RECALL/TICKET/HISTORY topic
    When the recovery process runs for this order
    Then the CreatedStateStrategy should handle the order
    And the recovery action should be REBUILD
    And the order should be rebuilt in the cache with state "New"
    And no DFD request should be sent


  Feature: Recovery of orders in Pending states
  As a system administrator
  I want orders in Pending states to be properly recovered
  So that the system can maintain consistent state after restart

  Background:
    Given the system is in recovery mode
    And the transaction logs are available

  Scenario: Order with state mismatch in PendingNew state is republished
    Given an order with ID "ORD-124" exists in transaction logs
    And the order has state "PendingNew" in RECALL/TICKET/HISTORY topic
    And the order has state "New" in RECALL/TO/OMS topic
    When the recovery process runs for this order
    Then the PendingStateStrategy should handle the order
    And the recovery action should be REPUBLISH
    And the ticket should be republished to RECALL/TICKET topic

  Scenario: Order with newer response in PendingCancel state is ignored
    Given an order with ID "ORD-125" exists in transaction logs
    And the order has state "PendingCancel" in RECALL/TICKET/HISTORY topic
    And the order has state "PendingCancel" in RECALL/TO/OMS topic with timestamp "2023-01-01T10:00:00Z"
    And the order has state "Canceled" in OMS/TO/RECALL topic with timestamp "2023-01-01T10:01:00Z"
    When the recovery process runs for this order
    Then the PendingStateStrategy should handle the order
    And the recovery action should be IGNORE
    And no action should be taken for the order

  Scenario: Order with consistent state in PendingFill state is rebuilt
    Given an order with ID "ORD-126" exists in transaction logs
    And the order has state "PendingFill" in RECALL/TICKET/HISTORY topic
    And the order has state "PendingFill" in RECALL/TO/OMS topic
    And the order has no entry in OMS/TO/RECALL topic
    When the recovery process runs for this order
    Then the PendingStateStrategy should handle the order
    And the recovery action should be REBUILD
    And the order should be rebuilt in the cache with state "PendingFill"
    And the ExecutionReport from RECALL/TO/OMS should be attached to the order



