Feature: DFD Request handling during recovery
  As a system administrator
  I want DFD requests to be sent for appropriate transitions during recovery
  So that the system's state is accurately reflected

  Background:
    Given the system is in recovery mode
    And the transaction logs are available

  Scenario: DFD request sent for PendingFill to Filled transition
    Given an order with ID "ORD-130" exists in transaction logs
    And the order has state "PendingFill" in RECALL/TICKET/HISTORY topic
    And the order has state "Filled" in OMS/TO/RECALL topic
    And the OMS/TO/RECALL entry has execType "2" (Filled)
    When the recovery process runs for this order
    Then the order should be rebuilt in the cache with state "Filled"
    And a DFD request should be sent to RECALL/TO/OMS topic

  Scenario: DFD request sent for PendingCancel to Canceled transition
    Given an order with ID "ORD-131" exists in transaction logs
    And the order has state "PendingCancel" in RECALL/TICKET/HISTORY topic
    And the order has state "Canceled" in OMS/TO/RECALL topic
    And the OMS/TO/RECALL entry has execType "4" (Canceled)
    When the recovery process runs for this order
    Then the order should be rebuilt in the cache with state "Canceled"
    And a DFD request should be sent to RECALL/TO/OMS topic



Feature: Default recovery strategy for unhandled states
  As a system administrator
  I want a fallback strategy for orders in unexpected states
  So that the system can handle all possible scenarios

  Background:
    Given the system is in recovery mode
    And the transaction logs are available

  Scenario: Order with unknown state uses default strategy
    Given an order with ID "ORD-132" exists in transaction logs
    And the order has state "UnknownState" in RECALL/TICKET/HISTORY topic
    When the recovery process runs for this order
    Then the DefaultRecoveryStrategy should handle the order
    And the recovery action should be REBUILD with warning about unknown state
    And the order should be rebuilt in the cache with state "UnknownState"



Feature: End-to-end recovery process
  As a system administrator
  I want the entire recovery process to work correctly
  So that the system can recover from failures

  Background:
    Given the system is in recovery mode
    And transaction logs contain multiple orders in different states

  Scenario: Recovery process rebuilds all orders in correct states
    When the recovery process runs for all orders
    Then all orders should be recovered with appropriate actions
    And recovery statistics should show accurate counts for each action type
    And all orders should be in correct states in the cache

  Scenario: Recovery process handles errors gracefully
    Given some transaction log entries are corrupted
    When the recovery process runs for all orders
    Then valid orders should be recovered correctly
    And errors should be logged for corrupted entries
    And the recovery process should continue for remaining orders


Feature: Transaction log reconstruction
  As a system administrator
  I want transaction logs to be correctly reconstructed from topic data
  So that recovery decisions are based on accurate information

  Background:
    Given the system is starting up
    And AMPS topics contain historical message data

  Scenario: Transaction logs are reconstructed from all topics
    When the transaction log reconstruction process runs
    Then the transaction logs should contain entries from RECALL/TICKET/HISTORY topic
    And the transaction logs should contain entries from RECALL/TO/OMS topic
    And the transaction logs should contain entries from OMS/TO/RECALL topic
    And each order should have a chronologically ordered log of events

  Scenario: Transaction log entries preserve message content
    When the transaction log reconstruction process runs
    Then each entry should preserve the original message content
    And RecallTicket objects should be retrievable from RECALL/TICKET/HISTORY entries
    And Order objects should be retrievable from RECALL/TO/OMS entries
    And ExecutionReport objects should be retrievable from OMS/TO/RECALL entries


Feature: Recovery context creation
  As a system component
  I want recovery contexts to be correctly created from transaction logs
  So that recovery strategies have accurate information

  Scenario: Recovery context contains the latest entry from each topic
    Given transaction logs exist for order "ORD-133"
    And the logs contain multiple entries for each topic
    When a recovery context is created for the order
    Then the context should contain the latest entry from RECALL/TICKET/HISTORY
    And the context should contain the latest entry from RECALL/TO/OMS
    And the context should contain the latest entry from OMS/TO/RECALL

  Scenario: Recovery context handles missing topic entries
    Given transaction logs exist for order "ORD-134"
    And the logs contain entries only for RECALL/TICKET/HISTORY
    When a recovery context is created for the order
    Then the context should contain the entry from RECALL/TICKET/HISTORY
    And the context should have null values for RECALL/TO/OMS
    And the context should have null values for OMS/TO/RECALL

                                                    
